WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.335
- I think most of your
audience can appreciate

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:05.638 align:start size:88% position:13%
that if you, as a
culture, had a monopoly

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the conversation for a
century, as progressives had,

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you start losing
control of that monopoly,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:14.514
it is going to look
like chaos to you.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
Your tension and fear
is going to be palpable,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.853
and that tension and fear
is going to be contagious.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.555 align:start size:97% position:3%
So some very, very bad
people are very, very worried

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.525
about losing their stature
and status in our society,

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.160
and that should make
right-thinking people

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.762
very, very happy.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.664
(mysterious music)

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.242 line:0%
- It's Locals week here
on the Rubin Report,

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.277 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and I'm doing mini
interviews with creators

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:47.714 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
on why they decided to become
less reliant on big tech

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.683
and instead own their
content and community

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.186
and livelihood with locals.com.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.423
Joining me today is the Willy
Wonka of politics himself.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.958
Michael Malice, welcome
back to the Rubin Report.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.993
- Thanks, Dave.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.161
- I thought you were going to be

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
in one of your Michael
Malice get ups,

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:06.800
dressed as Tulsi Gabbard
or Bea Arthur or somebody,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you're just giving
me regular Malice.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.237 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh no, I'm dressed like
the little mermaid right now.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.973
- From the bottom down.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.608
- That's the mermaid part, yeah.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.110
- That's the mermaid part.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.346
All right, Malice, before we
get into why you're on Locals,

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.349
and you've had incredible
success there actually,

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.553
I thought I should probably
give you a little credit

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:97% position:3%
because you've been
predicting the disintegration

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.624
of everything for quite some
time, and as a matter of fact,

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:35.195
you relish in it, but
also point to a way

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.163
that it will not
be all horrible,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.998
and I think that's what
people are worried about.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.500
Help me out with this.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- Yeah, I think most of
your audience can appreciate

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
that if you, as a
culture, had a monopoly

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:49.476 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
on the conversation for a
century, as progressives had,

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:52.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you start losing
control of that monopoly,

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.414
it is going to look
like chaos to you,

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:57.117
and your tension and fear
is going to be palpable,

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.586
and that tension and fear
is going to be contagious.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
So some very, very bad
people are very, very worried

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.625
about losing their stature
and status in our society,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that should make
right-thinking people
very, very happy.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:11.097 align:start position:0%
This should be something
that's an opportunity for hope.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.833
You know, you don't
tear down a building,

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.368
it's not like a snap of fingers

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.870
and then a new building's there.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.471
It is going to have to be
that transition period,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.906
which is going to be ugly.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.208
This ugliness is kind
of like an emetic.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.711
If you've ever had it
coming out both ends,

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.246
that's basically
what we're seeing.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
The body politic is purging
itself of the poison.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.518
- Yeah, what do you
think it looks like,

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.919
regardless of who wins?

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.021
Perhaps you want to
make a prediction.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.790
In a year from now, when
we get to that other side,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.660
the rebuild side, what do
you think that looks like?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.228
- Well, the beauty
of chaos is you have

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.063
no way of knowing what
it's going to look like.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:48.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we all remember in
2016, after Trump got elected,

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:81% position:19%
we were like, what
does this mean?

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:88% position:13%
None of us had any clue
what a Donald Trump

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.774
presidency would look like.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.476
On the one hand,
it could have been

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.344
like an Arnold Schwarzenegger
governorship of California,

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:88% position:13%
where he's kind of
this middle of the road

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.881
lefty Republican, and
ends up destroying

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.416
the Republican party forever,

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:08.354
or he could have gone full
Giuliani plus law and order,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.723
let's bring out the wood
chippers or the guillotines

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.692
or whatever, and it's
kind of been a mix.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of it's much more
rhetorical than otherwise.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.797
The other concern
is we don't know

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
what a Biden presidency
would look like.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.667
There's two scenarios.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.603
One is Biden is gonna
be a moderate Democrat.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
Biden has been very
anti-crime in his career.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Biden is the one who
took down Bernie Sanders,

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.375
not President Trump.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.978
Or Biden is gonna be
weak and ineffectual,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.180
and Black Lives Matter
is basically gonna be

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.648
running the country
and Antifa's gonna be

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.751
running the country, and
the court's gonna be packed

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.353
and any kind of right wing gains

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.655 align:start size:84% position:16%
at a legal level
will be lost forever.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.724
Both of these scenarios
are also plausible there.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.159
We have no way of knowing.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
All I know is that people
who are comfortable

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start size:84% position:16%
are going to be
made uncomfortable,

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that, historically,
is a good thing.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.769
- But either way, you want less

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.304
of these people in our lives.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.106
Is that fair to say, Malice?

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, so when
they're running around

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.109
like chickens with
their heads cut off,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
possibly, hopefully literally,
that is going to be good

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.414
because when they're
fighting each other

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.316
and they can't get
their stuff together,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.552 align:start size:84% position:16%
that gives them less
of an opportunity

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.487 align:start size:84% position:16%
to try to inflict
their schemes on us.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.489
And here's another
thing that should be

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.658
very, very exciting
for a lot of people.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.593
Ron Paul, and then
President Trump,

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.229 align:start size:84% position:16%
have legitimized the
anti-war position

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.697
within the Republican party,

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.734 align:start size:97% position:3%
which had been the case before
with the rise of neocons,

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.002
and George. W. Bush especially,

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.504 align:start size:84% position:16%
became part and parcel
of Republicanism.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
Imagine if Joe Biden,
without some sort

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.576
of enormous 9/11 event,
or even maybe with one,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.545
God forbid, or President
Trump in a second term

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.414
said we're all going to war.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:97% position:3%
He would not have the ability
to form that coalition

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
that historically
past presidents have.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.555 align:start size:88% position:13%
So to have that chaos
and that lack of ability

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.291
to form a consensus
is, in this case,

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.893
literally saving hundreds
of thousands of lives.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.162
- Well, Malice, it's
that sort of insight.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.430
That's why I love you.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.732
That's why I quote
you all the time.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:03.636 align:start size:88% position:13%
You've been an odd voice
of reason, somehow,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
in these crazy times, and
your book is right over there,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.440
right off camera right now.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.244 align:start size:97% position:3%
Anyhoo, this is a good segue
to why you're on Locals,

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:14.580
because you were the
third person on there.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.082
I hand selected you.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.850
I said this guy will be perfect,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.152
when we were just
sort of seeding it,

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.888
just to who could
be the test people.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:25.792 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why did you think that
doing something off big tech

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.560
was gonna be good for you?

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.697
- It was such a no brainer.

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.165
I was looking for
an alternative.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.702
I was on Patreon before,
and here are the advantages

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.203
I had with Locals.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:41.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
I do not ever have to worry
that I'm going to make a video

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.811 align:start size:97% position:3%
or send out a tweet and
have everything I've created

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.279
vanished overnight.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:48.247 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't have to worry about
not having a recourse.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.982
First of all, I could call
you, or you would call me

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.084 align:start size:84% position:16%
and be like, hey,
this is inappropriate.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.618
Let's figure this out.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.821
Number one, I have a call
in to the guy at the top.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:56.222
Number two is ...

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.224 align:start size:97% position:3%
- For the record, I certainly
won't say that to you.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.158
It's your site.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.727
We're just giving you the tools.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.962 align:start size:97% position:3%
What you do with those tools
is up to you, my friend.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.464
- Do you want to play this fire,

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.733 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we can play
with this fire.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, in all seriousness,
that was a huge advantage.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:13.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Second, the vibe of
Locals is this was a place

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.508
where me and people
who like what I do

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.344
and respect what
I do are welcome,

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.781 line:0%
as opposed to being regarded
as something to put up with

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:24.784 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and an embarrassment and
something to apologize about.

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:27.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I don't think people
appreciate to what extent

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.689 align:start size:88% position:13%
the employees at,
let's suppose, Spotify,

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:34.660 align:start size:97% position:3%
are driven crazy that their
platform is being used

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.597
to further the views of
people that they regard

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:40.633
as literal Nazis, or
Twitter, or Facebook.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.503
So when you have that
kind of disconnect

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.438
between the people
running the site

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.807
and the creators,
who are Jewish,

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's very reassuring to
know you're not gonna have

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
to sit down with
someone and explain,

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.649
no I would have been
against the holocaust,

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.551
and would have been a victim.

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.920
- Yeah, so part of
this, of course,

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.522
is that there's a pay wall.

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:05.958
You have a minimum, right,
but you let people come on

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.927
for whatever they want to pay.

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.762
I know some people must be
saying, but wait a minute,

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
Michael Malice wrote a book
called "The New Right".

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:14.467
He's an expert at what
the trolls are up to.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.702
Why would he want
to be in a place

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:20.239
where there are no trolls,
because trolls won't pay you?

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:21.908
- All my followers are trolls.

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.309
I'm a professional troll.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:26.045 align:start size:88% position:13%
I trolled Kamala Harris
very successfully.

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:28.614
I troll people all
the time on Twitter.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:31.517
Trolling, at its best,
is the art of exploiting

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:34.020
someone's weaknesses and
turning them to former

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.788
for the sake of the
broader audience.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:38.524 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is impish, it is
mischievous, it is fun,

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.493
it is very much Willy Wonka,

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.829 align:start size:81% position:19%
but it's not about
being hateful.

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:45.631 align:start size:97% position:3%
Me just telling you, hey
Dave, you're an SOB or that,

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not trolling,
that's just being a jerk.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:51.437
So I think people enjoy,
my followers certainly,

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:54.407
the people who support
me, enjoy how effective

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:57.877
puncturing these balloons
are of these pompous people

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:59.779
who have presumed to put
themselves in positions

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:02.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
of authority despite being
such mediocre people.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:04.851 align:start size:88% position:13%
Here's one great example
I frequently use.

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:08.087
I'll just ask them, have you
ever considered the possibility

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:10.189
that you're the bad guys?

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.592
Just that one simple
question to the likes

00:08:12.592 --> 00:08:16.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
of these operatives
really gets people excited

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:20.266
and gets some of them to
wonder, do you know what?

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.934
Maybe I don't have it
as much figured out

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.336
as I'd like to think I do.

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:25.471
- Yeah, do you think the
ship has totally sailed

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
with big tech, that
we're basically

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.141
just at the end of it now?

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.712
We all are on borrowed
time there, basically?

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:37.717
- No, but I think that any
time you have any industry,

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:39.986
it's going to at first ossify

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:42.889 align:start size:84% position:16%
into four to 10
major establishments.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:44.290
It was the case in publishing.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.691
It had six companies.

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:47.159
It's the case in music.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.528
They had a certain
number of labels.

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:50.796
But after a certain
time, like in music,

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.566 align:start size:88% position:13%
like in self publishing
and the internet,

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:55.735
they might have a
disproportionate
amount of impact

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:57.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the market, but
they're not going to have

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:01.574 align:start position:0%
that monopoly control that
we're seeing to some extent now.

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:04.176 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's very few people
who are completely

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.178
driven off the internet.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
The rest, they're
having issues with it.

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:11.551 align:start size:97% position:3%
The fact that you're creating
a competitive alternative

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:14.987
to them really is an
issue because just

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:18.057 align:start size:84% position:16%
if I'm not political,
if I could choose

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:21.060
between Patreon and Locals,
and they're both comparable

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.462
in their advantages, but
this has the disadvantage

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.498 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I might lose
my account overnight

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:27.967
for some political
reason, whereas here

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:29.502
that's not gonna be a concern,

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:32.305
and I'm gonna have a similar
ability to track audiences,

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:33.973
why wouldn't I go
to this other one?

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.776
- Have you booted anyone out
of your Locals community yet?

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:38.377
- I have not ever had to.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:39.979
I've never had to warn anyone.

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:42.014
I mean having that velvet rope,

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.683
how I have it set
up is it's free.

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:45.384 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you want to watch,
read everything,

00:09:45.384 --> 00:09:46.886
